          "create_time": 1794518070.199,
          "update_time": 1794518071.583,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The exact sum has a useful structure: it is an autocorrelation of one Dirichlet polynomial. I’m testing whether a mean-square estimate can preserve the cancellation across shifts. The key issue is whether it applies to the actual weighted, cutoff arm; a bound for the full zeta function alone would leave that transfer unproved.\n"
            ]
          },
