          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "I have a promising alternative that appears to bypass the joint theorem’s shift restriction. A Mellin projection can recover the exact weighted, cutoff Dirichlet arm from zeta, so a published mean-square error bound may control the combined signed correlation. I’m checking the cutoff kernel and its tails before claiming a shorter-window result.\n"
            ]
          },
