          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The calculation now gives a candidate window exponent of \\(17/81\\approx0.20988\\), improving on \\(17/72\\approx0.23611\\). The estimate controls the real part of the full quadratic correlation—the quantity the tail norm actually uses. I’m checking that distinction carefully, along with the revised head cutoffs; it does not give a pointwise Green bound.\n"
            ]
